Resend started with sending. In 2025, we added[receiving](https://resend.com/blog/inbound-emails) , so your app could get mail, too. Webhooks fire, but the rest is up to you.


"The rest" turned out to be a lot of work. Once email comes in, someone has to read it, sort it, reply to it, and remember where the conversation left off. Increasingly, that someone is an agent.


## The inbox for agents


Today we're announcing[Inboxes](https://resend.com/products/inboxes) .


Built for agents, but ready for your whole team.


An inbox sends and receives email at an address on one of your domains, like` support@example.com` . Every message is grouped into a thread, and every thread is available to your app, your team, and your agents.


Share an inbox with your team, assign conversations, leave notes, and pick up where someone else left off. The **same inbox can be worked by people and agents** side by side.


## Ready for every use case


You can build and use Inboxes to fit any use case.


- **Agents** : give each AI agent its own address to receive tasks, approvals, and updates.
- **Support** : route support email into your product and fetch threads through the API.
- **Assistant** : let an agent sort incoming requests, draft replies, and keep threads moving.
- **Recruiting** : create an inbox for teams and agents to track candidate conversations.
- **On-call** : collect alerts in one inbox and assign each one, so nothing sits unassigned.
- **Notifications** : send receipts, alerts, and updates for your app to process.


## Build inboxes your way


Inboxes are API-first. Create an inbox, list conversations as they arrive, and reply from your app, an agent, or an automated workflow.


