## Primitives built for the inbox


To support building custom experiences, we're releasing a full set of primitives centered on the inbox experience.


- **Folders** for inbox, archive, spam, trash, and sent.
- **Search** with a Gmail-like query syntax, plus sender and date filters.
- **Labels** for tagging and organizing threads.
- **Drafts** for collaborating on emails before sending them.
- **Forwarding** and **reply all** , with CC, BCC, and[idempotency keys](https://resend.com/docs/dashboard/emails/idempotency-keys) .
- **Webhooks** for everything from` inbox.email.received` to` inbox.thread.assigned` .
- **Agent settings** for configuring the built-in agent instructions, tone, and actions.


## Ready for your agents


Connect the agents you already use, like Claude Code, Cursor, Codex, Grok, or Gemini, through[MCP](https://resend.com/docs/mcp-server) or[skills](https://resend.com/docs/resend-skill) .


Build, manage, and triage inboxes with your agents using the API, CLI, or MCP server.


Ask your agent to summarize what came in overnight, find the invoice from last month, or draft a reply to the customer who's been waiting since Tuesday.


## Customizable UI layer


The inbox UI includes built-in agents that can build custom, dynamic views of emails and threads to fit your needs.


## Put your inbox on autopilot


You can also customize built-in agents to help you triage, organize, and respond to email.


Through the dashboard or via the API, give it instructions, a tone, and the actions it's allowed to take. It handles routine email work as it arrives, triggered by webhooks.


